<title>SWITZERLAND: Swiss set terms on one-year money market claims.</title>
<headline>Swiss set terms on one-year money market claims.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1997-01-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Swiss federal government set a 1.72 percent yield on its latest serices A.371 one-year money market funds based on a uniform price of 98.291, the Swiss National Bank said.</p>
<p>The allocation of 450.7 million Swiss francs will follow settlement on January 30.</p>
<p>The previous issue of three-month claims series 3.370, paid for January 23, raised 1,109.75 million francs and was priced at 99.607 to yield 1.561 percent annually.</p>
<p>-- Zurich editorial, +41 1 258 7340</p>
</text>
